# Chefaa Final Medications Overview (Products 1401–Final) — Extraction Blueprint and Execution Plan

## Executive Summary and Objectives

This blueprint sets out a complete, end-to-end plan to assemble, enrich, and validate a final pharmaceutical dataset covering Chefaa’s medications catalog with a specific focus on products 1401 onward. The target output is a single, authoritative JSON dataset: data/overviews/medications_final/medications_overview_final.json. The dataset will integrate evidence from Chefaa’s medications category and product detail pages, corroborated with the closest available product pages to ensure field coverage, consistency, and clinical fidelity.

Scope and inventory. The source corpus comprises 130 page files (pages 1–134), with well-documented gaps and zero-result ranges. Aggregated inventory indicates 2,280 discovered products. After deduplication and canonicalization, the tail slice (products ≥1401) is estimated at 880 records. Nine subcategory summaries (168 products) provide category hints and cross-checks, and several validated product detail exemplars anchor field mapping and pricing baselines.[^2]

Narrative arc. We begin by documenting the dataset origin and inventory posture. We then define the target product sequence (≥1401), including enumeration rules and a canonical anchor (ديكونادال). Next, we formalize the data model and schema, then detail extraction methods, validation pipelines, and the production write plan. Finally, we codify quality assurance, risks and mitigations, and acceptance criteria, followed by a concrete milestone plan to deliver a robust, clinically credible dataset.

Key deliverable. A single, versioned JSON dataset capturing identification, commercial, clinical, regulatory, and provenance fields for products ≥1401, with auditable source links, validated categories, and normalized brand and dosage attributes.

To orient scope and readiness, the following snapshot summarizes the posture of this plan.

