## Source Data Landscape and Inventory

The dataset is grounded in two complementary asset types: (1) 130 page-based JSON files that enumerate products per pagination index, and (2) nine subcategory summaries capturing curated product lists by therapeutic segment. Several mid-range pagination gaps and zero-result ranges are documented and factored into the plan.

Table 2. File and Coverage Summary
| Category of Evidence | File Naming Pattern | Approximate Count | Product Count | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Page-based files | medications_page_X_*.json | 130 | 2,280 | Core inventory; pages 1–134; gaps include 5, 6, 7, 68; zero-result pages 55–61, 73–83 |
| Subcategory summaries | subcategories within medications_products.json | 9 groups | 168 | Overlaps likely with page files; useful for taxonomy hints and cross-validation |
| Category landing evidence | Screenshots | N/A | N/A | Visual corroboration of category and product pages used to design extraction[^2][^4][^6] |

The most efficient path to the target sequence is to enumerate page-based files in ascending order, deduplicate and canonicalize, and then slice to products ≥1401. Subcategory summaries support controlled vocabulary mapping and provide fallback enrichment where product detail content is intermittently inaccessible.

